  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Quiet Architectural Frame",
    "overview": "The interface gives a warm modern house room to be seen. Pale stone surfaces, charcoal type, and a forest primary control form a restrained working frame; timber, planting, glass, and water belong to the three-dimensional architecture. The experience is a compact concept viewer rather than a marketing page.\n\nDensity stays measured and useful: short room labels, small familiar controls, and readable context around a dominant model. The project title leads directly, without an introductory kicker. This records the implemented warm modern direction in [the surface contract](.impeccable/surface.md); new surfaces should inherit its materials and restraint rather than its exact composition.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Pale stone framing with a single forest action color.",
      "Dedicated display type for project identity; compact sans type for operation.",
      "Flat, lightly bordered controls around a richly modeled scene.",
      "Immediate room, camera, and walkthrough feedback."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Material Ownership Rule",
        "body": "Keep oak, glass, and water as material information; use forest for interface action.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Identity Pair Rule",
        "body": "Reserve House Display for the project heading and wordmark; keep operational labels in the body stack.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Frame Rule",
        "body": "Use tonal separation for resting controls; reserve the documented shadow for the floating help panel.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** keep material colors tied to architecture and forest tied to interface action.",
      "**Do** preserve opaque labels and clear focus outlines over the changing scene.",
      "**Do** use the dedicated display face for project identity and the body stack for controls.",
      "**Do** adapt control density and navigation to narrow and short viewports.",
      "**Do** honor reduced motion in both UI transitions and camera movement."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** introduce a kicker above the project title.",
